    "reading_order": 3,
    "text": "Example 9 : Harpreet tosses two different coins simultaneously (say, one is of ` 1\nand other of ` 2). What is the probability that she gets at least one head?",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH114",
    "page": 9,
    "block_id": "jemh114_p009_b04",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      126.99,
      420.04,
      192.47
    ],
    "reading_order": 4,
    "text": "Solution : We write H for ‘head’ and T for ‘tail’. When two coins are tossed\nsimultaneously, the possible outcomes are (H, H), (H, T), (T, H), (T, T), which are all\nequally likely. Here (H, H) means head up on the first coin (say on ` 1) and head up\non the second coin (` 2). Similarly (H, T) means head up on the first coin and tail up on\nthe second coin and so on.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH114",
